# Conformance probe pack for an `if` and an `opt` at the end of a `length`
# extent (spec 0.21 ruling 31), most significant bit first. Public. No kinds.
#
#   p           one presence bit, then 7 unused bits
#   block 1     an 8-bit length in bytes: x in 8 bits; when p.1 is 1, nums to
#               the end of the block (val in 8 bits each)
#   block 2     an 8-bit length in bytes: y in 8 bits; an opt bit, then 7
#               unused bits and recs to the end of the block (x in 8 bits)
format     conformance-extents-walk
version    0.21.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
layout     sequential
bit_order  msb
presence p 1
pad 7
length 8
  field  probe.x  8  uint
  if p.1
    group  probe.nums rest
      field  probe.val  8  uint
    end
  end
end
length 8
  field  probe.y  8  uint
  opt
    pad 7
    group  probe.recs rest
      field  probe.x  8  uint
    end
  end
end
